.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead resolve" 1  "bead resolve " 
.SH NAME
bead resolve \- Record an execution attempt outcome atomically
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead resolve\fR [\fB\-\-action\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-revision\fR] [\fB\-\-fencing\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-evidence\-ref\fR] [\fB\-\-actor\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-\-harness\fR] [\fB\-\-harness\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-attempt\-id\fR> <\fB\-\-outcome\fR> <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolve an execution attempt by recording its outcome and applying
a lifecycle transition in one atomic operation. This implements the
attempt\-outcome\-v1 specification with exactly\-once semantics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-attempt\-id\fR \fI<ATTEMPT_ID>\fR
Attempt ID (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-outcome\fR \fI<OUTCOME>\fR
Outcome classification (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fI<ACTION>\fR
Lifecycle action to apply
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Human\-readable reason for the action
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-revision\fR \fI<IF_REVISION>\fR
Expected revision for optimistic concurrency control
.TP
\fB\-\-fencing\-token\fR \fI<FENCING_TOKEN>\fR
Fencing token for lease validation
.TP
\fB\-\-evidence\-ref\fR \fI<EVIDENCE_REF>\fR
Evidence references (NAMESPACE:VALUE format)
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\fR \fI<ACTOR>\fR [default: unknown]
Actor identity
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
Model identifier for telemetry
.TP
\fB\-\-harness\fR \fI<HARNESS>\fR
Harness name for telemetry
.TP
\fB\-\-harness\-version\fR \fI<HARNESS_VERSION>\fR
Harness version for telemetry
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output format
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Issue ID
